# Mass run

- This subsystem stores named container-run presets (`name`, `container_name`, `port`, `label`, `env_vars`) in the separate mass-run SQLite database.
- Preset CRUD and whole-set replacement stay on the existing `/massrun/*` handlers. Clients execute the saved set through `POST /massrun/execute` (`image_name`); they must not loop `POST /docker/container/run`.
- Execute loads presets in list order (`created_at` DESC), starts each sequentially via `container.RunFromRequest`, and continues after individual failures. HTTP 200 with `started` and `failed[{name,detail}]` covers total and partial success; empty presets and missing `image_name` are 400.
- Environment variables are persisted as JSON and exposed as maps in shared API types.
- Preserve atomic replacement semantics for bulk import: a failed replacement must not leave a partially updated set.
- Container request-field changes must stay aligned with mass-run storage and YAML import/export in the web client.
- Verify execute with `go test ./internal/handlers/massrun/...` (mock `runFromRequest`; no Docker daemon).
